Package: ssdiff
Title: Supervised Semantic Differential
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Paweł", "Lenartowicz", email = "pawellenartowicz@europe.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Hubert", "Plisiecki", email = "hplisiecki@gmail.com",
           role = "aut"),
    person("Jason", "Miller", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "Preact (MIT licence), bundled in inst/page_template.html"),
    person("Google Inc.", role = "cph",
           comment = "htm (Apache-2.0 licence), bundled in inst/page_template.html")
    )
Description: Interpretable, embedding-based analysis of concept meaning in
    text. Builds per-document concept vectors from local contexts around
    seed words, learns a semantic gradient that predicts a numeric outcome
    or separates groups, and interprets it through the nearest neighbours of
    each pole, clusters of those neighbours, text snippets and per-document
    scores. The method is described in Plisiecki, Lenartowicz, Pokropek,
    Małyska and Flakus (2025) <doi:10.31234/osf.io/gvrsb_v1>. A port of the
    'Python' package 'ssdiff'.
